  "run": {
    "final_text": "I added the v2.4.0 entry to the top of `RELEASE_NOTES.md`. It matches the format of the earlier entries, and the version and date come from `VERSION` and `RELEASE_DATE`:\n\n```\nv2.4.0 - 2026-10-20\n  * BREAKING: Remove deprecated --legacy flag from sync (ACME-421)\n  * CSV exporter for the report command (ACME-412)\n  * Retry uploads on 503 with backoff (ACME-415)\n  * Fix crash when config file is empty (ACME-419)\n  * Fix wrong totals in monthly summary for leap years (ACME-423)\n```\n\n**Decision for you:** ACME-421 is marked as breaking (the `!`) because it removes the `--legacy` flag. Under semantic versioning, a breaking change would normally make this 3.0.0, not 2.4.0. I left `VERSION` at 2.4.0 and listed the change first with a \"BREAKING:\" label. If you'd rather bump to 3.0.0, the heading needs to change along with `VERSION`.\n\nI left out PR authors because the earlier entries don't list them.",
